+## parallel_merge_sort: OpenMP project Merge Sort
+
+The separate configurable registry contains merge_sort and parallel_merge_sort;
+normal sorting registry/default semantics are preserved. Public
+parallel_merge_sort(Values&,int) returns actual team size/parallel-region status.
+Stable signed-int32 output, requests1..64, no nested OpenMP invocation. One N-key
+buffer is allocated before mutation/task entry; allocation errors propagate.
+N<32768 or request1 uses allocation-free serial merging after that allocation.
+Otherwise a single OpenMP team starts tied child tasks at halves above grain16384;
+taskwait precedes each parent merge/copy. Child value/buffer ranges are disjoint.
+Only nonthrowing int32 operations run inside tasks; runtime creation failures are
+not claimed recoverable. No global counters or ICV mutation. Explicit test-only
+observers verify tasks/bounds/stability; normal production uses an empty observer.
+
+Work O(N log N), auxiliary O(N) plus task/team runtime memory and bounded range
+recursion. Parent merges are serial. This is a top-down task implementation with
+bottom-up serial leaves and copy-back merges, distinct from the preserved
+alternating-buffer sequential Merge Sort. Its request1 time is therefore a separate
+implementation baseline; do not conflate it with sequential Merge Sort speedup.
+No counted adapter or isolated allocation measurement is implemented for it.
+
+The [versioned contract](OPENMP_PROTOCOL_v1.md) defines synchronization and test
+policy. OpenMP specifies [task execution](https://www.openmp.org/spec-html/5.2/openmpse73.html)
+and [taskwait synchronization](https://www.openmp.org/spec-html/5.2/openmpse93.html).
+Correctness stress and disjoint ownership review do not prove absence of races;
+actual race-detector outcomes are recorded in AUDIT.md.
